3. Shared Layout & Theme Implementation
   Theme Colors: Navbar and Sidebar use the dark green theme (#173b35, hover: #24564b), while the central workspace uses light gray-green (#f3f5f4) with white cards (#ffffff) and soft borders (#e1e7e4).
   Fixed Layout Geometry:
   Navbar: fixed top-0 left-0 lg:left-[250px] right-0 h-[68px] z-30
   Sidebar: fixed top-0 bottom-0 left-0 w-[250px] z-50
   MainContent: ml-0 lg:ml-[250px] mt-[68px] min-h-[calc(100vh-68px)] flex-1 overflow-y-auto
   Navigation:
   Supports active-route highlighting via NavLink.
   Expandable nested accordion for Production & Quality.
   Accommodates future modules (Sales, Engineering, Inventory, HRMS) with badge indicators.
   Responsive mobile drawer with backdrop overlay.
4. Production & Quality Pages & Features (Module M4)
   Production Dashboard (/production-quality/production):
   KPI metrics (Total Orders, In Progress, On Hold, Completed).
   Work center workload capacity indicators (Line 1 Cutting, Precision Lathes, Galvanizing).
   Active work orders table with progress bars.
   Work Orders Page (/production-quality/work-orders):
   Filter chips by lifecycle state (DRAFT, PLANNED, READY_FOR_PRODUCTION, IN_PROGRESS, ON_HOLD, COMPLETED, CANCELLED).
   Search by WO#, product, or customer name.
   Interactive + Create Work Order modal dialog.
   Work Order Details Page (/production-quality/work-orders/:id):
   Real-time stock check against inventory.
   Lifecycle transition triggers (Submit, Approve, Release, Start, Hold, Resume, Cancel).
   Log Production Output modal.
   Transfer to Quality Inspection modal.
   Bill of materials component tracking & audit history timeline.
   Production Planning Page (/production-quality/planning):
   Monthly production calendar with scheduled runs.
   Shift capacity utilization (Shift A 92%, Shift B 74%, Shift C 30%).
   Raw material staging checklist.
   Quality Dashboard (/production-quality/quality):
   Quality metrics (Inspections, Pass rate, On Hold, NCRs).
   Pending inspection queue snapshot.
   Defect category breakdown chart.
   Standard compliance checklist (IS-3043 / IEC 62561).
   Inspections Queue Page (/production-quality/inspections):
   Live inspection queue with status badges.
   Inspect modal with accepted/rejected quantity counters and tolerance notes.
   Idempotent Release to Finished Goods dialog with warehouse location and batch assignment.
   Non-Conformance Page (/production-quality/non-conformance):
   Open Non-Conformance Reports (NCR) with severity badges (CRITICAL, MAJOR, MINOR).
   Log New NCR modal with immediate containment action.
   Authorize Scrap Write-Off modal with financial cost impact.
5. Multi-Developer Collaboration Model

The project is structured to prevent Git merge conflicts across 5 team members:

Developer 1 (Integration / Layout): Controls src/app/router.jsx, src/app/routeRegistry.js, and src/components/layout/.
Developer 2 (Production & Quality): Works exclusively in src/features/production_quality/ and exports routes in productionQualityRoutes.jsx.
Developer 3 (Sales): Works in src/features/sales/ and registers routes into src/app/routeRegistry.js.
Developer 4 (Engineering): Works in src/features/engineering/.
Developer 5 (Inventory): Works in src/features/inventory/. 6. Verification Results
